{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass on the third day, when it was morning.</b> This is the third day of separation (from their women) and the sixth of the month. <br><b>And it came to pass that there were voices and lightnings and a heavy cloud upon the mountain.</b> The voices were the voices of the angels who praise the Holy One, blessed be He, every morning, as is said (Job 38:7): ״ברן יחד כוכבי בקר ויריעו כל בני אלהים״, and the lightnings are angels as well, as is said (Psalms 104:4): ״עושה מלאכיו רוחות משרתיו אש לוהט״, and it is written (Ezekiel 1:13): ״ונוגה כאש ומן האש יוצא ברק״. And a heavy cloud, in order to separate between Israel and the angels, for if Israel had seen them they would have trembled at the sight of them; and thus it is written in Ezekiel (ibid.): ״ענן גדול ואש מתלקחת ומתוכה דמות ארבע חיות״. This is what our Master Hananel wrote, although the plain sense is true and established, and it is the first of the seventy faces, for the day of the giving of the Torah was like a cloudy day with voices — that is, thunder — in the manner of the world, and lightnings and some rain; and so it is written (Judges 5:4): ״ארץ רעשה גם שמים נטפו גם עבים נטפו מים״, and the cloud was first, then the lightnings, then the voices. And that which is last in the verse was first in occurrence, for it is customary to see the lightning and afterward the thunder. And the fact that Scripture mentioned them not in order appears to me to be for this reason: that He did so to elevate the sound of the shofar, for had He mentioned them in order, He would have placed the voices immediately next to the sound of the shofar, and it would have appeared that they were equal or close to one another in rank. Therefore He wished to put the voices first in order to distance them from the sound of the shofar and to make clear that there is a great distance and difference between them, like the difference between a physical thing and an intelligible thing."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:11.039297142Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}